# Issue: joinCtxsNG grouped the joinable predicates with joinByFst, which
# sorts the groups by key, and the key's Ord (class, then types) is
# string-intern order; the order of the dictionary bindings a definition
# emits followed it, so a one-shot compile and a `bsc -u` batch differed.
# Fix: Util.joinByFstStable keeps the groups in first-occurrence order.
# Probe: a reduced GrayCounter compiled alone, behind a scrambler that
# interns IsModule before Add, and under -trace-intern-reverse must dump
# the same .bo, hash included.

batching_bo_pair JoinOrder.bs JoinOrderRoot.bs JoinOrderScramble.bs
reverse_intern_same_bo JoinOrder.bs
